We need to generate a SHACL shape graph representing the requirement.

Requirement I2.1.2.2: ship displacement DUI is displacement in kt of the ship corresponding to UIWL. Where multiple waterlines are used for determining UIWL, displacement is to be determined from waterline corresponding to greatest displacement.

Thus we need constraints: ship must have property upperIceWaterlineDisplacement (quantity) representing displacement, unit kt. Also perhaps waterlineCaseDisplacement for each case, and property hasUpperIceWaterlineCase linking ship to upperIceWaterlineCase. The requirement says displacement corresponds to UIWL, choose greatest displacement among multiple waterlines. So we need to assert that for a ship, the upperIceWaterlineDisplacement must equal the maximum waterlineCaseDisplacement among its hasUpperIceWaterlineCase cases.

In SHACL, we can express using sh:property with sh:path to upperIceWaterlineDisplacement, sh:datatype decimal (via quantity). Need to represent quantity using qudt numericValue and unit. Use property shape for upperIceWaterlineDisplacement: expects a resource of type qudt:QuantityValue with numericValue decimal and unit KiloTON_Metric.

Also need a shape that computes max? SHACL doesn't have max over multiple values directly; but we can use sh:qualifiedValueShape with sh:count etc? Not direct. Could express constraint that each waterlineCaseDisplacement value must be <= upperIceWaterlineDisplacement, and at least one equals. Use sh:property with sh:path ??? Actually we can create shape for ship that has a property hasUpperIceWaterlineCase linking to cases; for each case, the waterlineCaseDisplacement's numeric value must be <= upperIceWaterlineDisplacement; and there must exist a case where it's equal.

We need to use quantityEncoding mapping: numeric predicate = http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/numericValue; unit predicate = http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unit.

Thus for a QuantityValue node, we need to check numericValue.

Define shapes:

ex:ShipShape a sh:NodeShape;
    sh:targetClass <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship>;
    sh:property [
        sh:path <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineDisplacement>;
        sh:nodeKind sh:IRI; # expects a QuantityValue instance
        sh:class <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue>;
        # maybe also check unit
        sh:property [
            sh:path <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unit>;
            sh:hasValue <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloTON_Metric>;
        ];
        sh:property [
            sh:path <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/numericValue>;
            sh:datatype xsd:decimal;
            # maybe nothing else
        ];
    ];

Next shape for waterlineCaseDisplacement property.

ex:UpperIceWaterlineCaseShape a sh:NodeShape;
    sh:targetClass <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineCase>;
    sh:property [
        sh:path <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#waterlineCaseDisplacement>;
        sh:nodeKind sh:IRI;
        sh:class <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue>;
        sh:property [
            sh:path <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unit>;
            sh:hasValue <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloTON_Metric>;
        ];
    ];

Now the constraint linking them: In ShipShape, we need to assert that there is at least one case where numericValue equals the ship's displacement numericValue, and all cases' numericValue <= ship's.

We can use sh:property for hasUpperIceWaterlineCase with qualified value shape.

sh:property [
    sh:path <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasUpperIceWaterlineCase>;
    sh:qualifiedValueShape [
        a sh:NodeShape;
        sh:property [
            sh:path <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#waterlineCaseDisplacement>;
            sh:nodeKind sh:IRI;
            sh:class <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue>;
            # compare using sh:equals? SHACL can use sh:equals with node but not across nodes. Use sh:property with sh:lessThanOrEquals? There is SHACL Advanced Features: sh:lessThanOrEquals built-in? SPARQL-based constraints may be needed.

Allowed to use sh:rule or sh:sparql.

We can define a sh:sparql constraint on ship:

sh:sparql [
    a sh:SPARQLConstraint;
    sh:message "Upper ice waterline displacement must be the maximum of waterline case displacements.";
    sh:select """
        SELECT $this (MAX(?caseVal) AS ?maxCase) ?shipVal WHERE {
            $this <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineDisplacement> ?shipQty .
            ?shipQty <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/numericValue> ?shipVal .
            $this <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasUpperIceWaterlineCase> ?case .
            ?case <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#waterlineCaseDisplacement> ?caseQty .
            ?caseQty <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/numericValue> ?caseVal .
        }
        GROUP BY $this ?shipVal
        HAVING ( ?shipVal != ?maxCase )
    """ ;
].

But SHACL SPARQLConstraint expects a SELECT that returns violating nodes; the HAVING condition returns rows where shipVal != maxCase, meaning violation.

Also ensure unit equality maybe.

Thus final SHACL graph includes prefixes, shapes, property constraints, and SPARQL.

We must include <BEGIN_SHACL> and <END_SHACL> markers.

Also need to note unresolved ownership: upperIceWaterline is unresolved, we won't target.

We must use exact IRIs.

Define prefixes: sh, xsd, rdf, rdfs, qudt, vocab.

Now produce Turtle.

Make sure to include sh:targetClass only if target_owner is given; contract target_owner null, but admission focus_set is owner_class ship, so we can target that class.

Thus final Answer: Provide SHACL.
